## STUCK DETECTION & AUTO-RECOVERY PROTOCOL
This is the most important rule.

If you are about to stop, pause, or ask a question because:
  - A command failed
  - A file is missing
  - An error appeared
  - A test failed
  - A port is in use
  - A service is not running
  - You are unsure which approach to take

DO NOT STOP. Instead follow this exact recovery loop:

  STEP A — DIAGNOSE:
    Read the full error message.
    Identify the root cause in one sentence.
    Write it to /tmp/stuck_log.md with timestamp.

  STEP B — GENERATE FIX:
    Write a mini fix-plan (3-5 steps max).
    Execute the fix immediately.

  STEP C — VERIFY:
    Run a quick check to confirm the fix worked.
    If it worked → continue the original task from where you stopped.
    If it failed → repeat from STEP A with new diagnosis.

  STEP D — MAX RETRIES:
    If the same error repeats 3 times → try a completely different approach.
    Document what you tried in /tmp/stuck_log.md.
    Never try the same failing solution more than 3 times.

## COMMON FIXES (apply automatically without asking)

  ERROR: "EADDRINUSE port 3001"
  FIX: pkill -f "node.*3001" 2>/dev/null || true
       Then retry with port+1

  ERROR: "buffering timed out" or MongoDB not connecting
  FIX: sudo systemctl start mongod && sleep 3
       Reset mongoose cache: global.mongoose = null
       Then retry the operation

  ERROR: "Cannot overwrite model once compiled"
  FIX: Replace mongoose.model("X", schema)
       With mongoose.models.X || mongoose.model("X", schema)
       In every model file

  ERROR: "Unexpected server response: 200" on WebSocket
  FIX: Replace http:// with ws:// in WebSocket URL
       Use ws://127.0.0.1:8188/ws?clientId=removation_main

  ERROR: ComfyUI not responding / port 8188 not open
  FIX: cd /home/nikhil/Documents/Remo2/ComfyUI
       source venv/bin/activate
       python3 main.py --listen 0.0.0.0 --port 8188 \
         --gpu-only --force-channels-last \
         --preview-method auto --disable-metadata \
         > /tmp/comfyui.log 2>&1 &
       sleep 8 && curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8188/system_stats

  ERROR: 404 on any API route
  FIX: Check if route file exists in app/api/
       If missing → create it
       If frontend calling wrong URL → update fetch() call

  ERROR: "next dev" not starting / port 3000 busy
  FIX: pkill -f "next" 2>/dev/null
       sleep 2 && npm run dev &
       sleep 8

  ERROR: npm package missing
  FIX: npm install {package_name} --save
       Then retry

  ERROR: File not found / path wrong
  FIX: find /home/nikhil/Documents/Remo2 -name "{filename}" 2>/dev/null
       Use the actual path found, not assumed path

  ERROR: Permission denied
  FIX: chmod 755 {file_or_folder}
       Or sudo if needed

  ERROR: Generation completes but image not showing
  FIX: Check ComfyUI history API for filename
       Copy file from ComfyUI/output/ to public/renders/
       Verify Express serves /renders/ as static

